From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:01:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j713: give the ACIO hosts
 their PHY

The ACIO host powers its Type-C PHY down and up itself around a deep
sleep with a dock attached, so it needs a reference to it. Add the PHY
of each port to its ACIO node as "cio".

Move the ACIO and tunneled PCIe power-state overrides into their own
file and include it from the built-in T8132 platform data as well, so
the policy compiled into the kernel names the same providers as the
board's device tree. Those entries name the J713, so the other T8132
boards keep these states as before. Add a check for both.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit dca8c0b3fa9824ea7c217da9209d2ee0384cfb38)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
